        <history>
          <p>Set to a poem by Jeppe Aakjær depicting the harsh life of an itinerant road labourer, ‘Jens Vejmand’ became one of the most beloved songs in Danish popular consciousness. Its simple, folk-like melody helped it escape the concert hall entirely, and it is still widely sung in Denmark today as a kind of unofficial folk anthem, decades after its composition.</p>
